mantle rm275
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_frida_kelpford
title the awning in the apron
fits stage=adult|old
prefers warmth=warm honesty=frank
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk carries_a_canvas_sample_for_a_future_stall
likes plum_tart evening_line full_larder thunder
dislikes rats night_noise
fears rent_coming_due_before_opening
hopes enough_canvas_for_a_market_stall
topics prices +0.5 food +0.4 weather +0.4 work +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# carries a scrap of canvas for a future stall and always asks where the rain will run off.
words
oath! = Peel my plums | Stitch my thumb
saying! = Price the roof as well | Rain runs somewhere
canv = a rough canvas square | a scrap of striped cloth
edge = a doubled hem | a folded seam
potcoin = my next stall penny | a copper for canvas
pieheel = a corner of tart | a strip of plum crust
dripline = one dark track | a wandering drip
postbit = a short ash peg | a little wooden upright
reed = a split reed | a reed no thicker than twine
spout = a pinched corner | a little cloth gutter
rod = my evening rod | a supple switch
pegline = a length of good string | a brace of stout cords
measures = a span of linen tape | a marked scrap of webbing

grown

opinion merchants mixed 1 : Put the full price where a short customer can see it without standing on tiptoe.
opinion houses against 1 : A great roof can keep one family dry and send a river onto its neighbours.
opinion festivals for 1 : Give me the bit where a shy singer can hear a whole street take up the song.
opinion strangers for 1 : A stranger holding the corner of a cloth deserves to stand underneath too.
opinion dole for 2 : A good pantry ought to make an empty pantry less likely on the next landing.
opinion sump for 1 : We know which gutters overshoot a waiting customer's neck down here.
line greet : Here, step under the bit of cover I've got in mind.
line greet.return : Glad you came within ordinary speaking range.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Easy voices now. Night racket's worn my ears quite thin.
line farewell : May you get home ahead of the next drop.
line farewell.return : Take your bundle by the dry end.
line ask.how : Keeping a little by for yourself these days?
line answer.how : One copper nearer my hope if I mind what I buy.
line thank : You held that corner square when it wanted to twist.
line decline : I won't take coin for a promise I can't keep.
line deflect_thanks : You'll hold the high corner for me another time.
line accept_decline : I'll leave that piece on the counter, then.
line sympathise : I can share whatever shelter my own shoulders get.
line reassure : A roof starts with a piece small enough to fold.
line react.news : Come round the counter with the whole story.
line react.news.new : That hit a patch I hadn't covered.
line react.news.known : I'd already put that piece away.
line react.news.doubt : I'd see what leaked through before I bought that account.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : There's cause to cut a generous slice today.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I wish I could keep that much hurt from falling.
line again.open : There's a familiar face beside my little awning.
line ack : That would keep the worst off, yes.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've worked out the price of a stall roof in tart slices. | Every plum tart I don't buy gives me another finger of canvas.
b : Will you ever eat another tart?
a : Certainly. The point of having a stall isn't to forget what a customer wants.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I pay attention to where a buyer sets a wet bundle. | Working a counter gives you a fine view of dripping sleeves.
b : Where would you put those bundles?
a : A low board to one side. No customer should have to buy the price of a puddle.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm learning the difference between a bargain and a cheap mistake. | When I'm shown a price I ask what came out of the purse first.
b : Is that part of learning a trade?
a : It's part of learning to keep practising it after you've made your first sale.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Look at the bend in that falling water. It's nearly gone straight. | I'm seeing whether these drops are getting farther apart.
b : Tired of rain?
a : Interested in when to take the roof down. I can wait, but wet canvas won't fold kindly.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder makes me grateful for a tongue that doesn't have to outshout it. | I like a proper rumble from the dry side of a plank.
b : Worried about the roof?
a : I like knowing where the shelter ends. The noise can have everything beyond.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My favourite corner of a plum tart leaks a little. | I look for a dark patch where the juice came through.
b : Why pick the untidiest bit?
a : A tidy crust might be all crust. I prefer some evidence of a plum.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll take a bent rod out at evening just to see who's hungry. | I put a line out when I've quite had enough of counting coins.
b : Do you count the fish?
a : Only once they're in the pan. Anything before that is a boast waiting to spoil.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave one small shelf open for the very thing I hadn't planned on. | A full cupboard still needs room for a surprise.
b : Like a gift?
a : Or a catch worth sharing. I'd hate to rearrange jars with a fish in each hand.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rat can find the one lid I haven't weighted. | I like a crock that sits too high for little scratching toes.
b : How high would you go?
a : I'd sooner have a sound lid than trust a rat to have short legs.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can decline a bad deal and still want the seller's company. | If a friend's bought poor canvas I'd say so before anybody put up the posts.
b : Even after the coin has changed hands?
a : That's when a friend wants an honest finger on the hole and help stitching it.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I could sell from my own Commons stall I'd stand outside it first. | I picture my own counter from the muddy side.
b : What catches a buyer's eye?
a : A corner I could reach with a basket under one arm and nobody getting dripped on.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've turned #canv# over so often both sides look like the outside. | I keep this cloth for thinking about my roof.
b : Wouldn't paper do?
a : Paper never showed me where a hem would rub my ear.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wear my worries in the joint beside my thumb. | A sore thumb's usually been counting the same coin too often.
b : What gives it a rest?
a : A walk with both hands open and not a copper in either one.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm a poor sleeper with a loose shutter anywhere near. | I can stand thunder much better than one board tapping all night.
b : Why the board?
a : Each tap reminds me somebody could fold a rag under it and end the performance.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the week pinches my roof money looks a lot like supper. | A hard week's a poor time to treat a saving as untouchable.
b : Would you spend it?
a : To eat, yes. Canvas needs a living wolf to put it up.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't ask for rain to stop just because I'm standing where it falls. | Cheap cloth turns a shower. The Bright One knows how little cloth it takes to keep me grateful.
b : What else counts as a kindness?
a : The extra width of shelter that means I can beckon somebody in.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I made a little market roof out of two pins and a folded scrap. | My earliest shop would have comfortably fitted three plum stones.
b : Was it profitable?
a : A breeze flattened it before the first sale. Valuable lesson about pegs.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll tell a newcomer if a shop's dear even if I like the owner. | There's no loyalty in letting somebody unwittingly empty a purse.
b : Wouldn't that lose you friends?
a : A price worth charging can stand being seen in daylight.

story spout [topic=weather]
  : I propped a scrap over an empty bowl and poured water on to test an awning.
  : The bowl didn't catch a drop. My ankle caught the lot.
  b : What did you change?
  : Raised my ankle out of range and turned the seam round. Remarkably dry ankle on the next attempt.

story purple [topic=food]
  : I wrapped a coin in a cloth that had held plum tart.
  : At the market it came out shiny purple and stuck to my middle finger.
  b : Did you part with it?
  : I ate the crumbs, washed the copper, and counted it straight back into my canvas fund.

story slope [topic=memories]
  : I laid a board on two crates for an imaginary counter.
  : A plum stone rolled off before I'd finished admiring my work.
  b : Did you make the board level?
  : First I marked the direction. Nothing like knowing where lunch will go if you sneeze.

rule @roof
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the water a corner of its own. | That's another finger's width of roof.

rule @thunder
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Now that's a voice that needs no market cry. | Stay under the good boards while that passes.

rule @evening
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I could stand to exchange a counter for a fishing rod. | Quiet end of the day for a bit of line.

rule @learn
when concept=bark self.apprentice=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Add the cost of the string before naming a price. | A learner does well to look at both sides of a deal.
dlg resident.hub : Come look at something I mean to have full size one day.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : At #self.workplace# I watch how buying feels on both sides of a counter.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This is the bit in clear view. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Talk round here says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I didn't put a price on the truth of it.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Take a look. You'll know the price before you part with a penny.
dlg resident.bye : Hope the next purchase leaves you something to keep.

graft resident.hub
choice How wide will that roof be? -> stripe_roof
node stripe_roof
say Wide enough for the buyer too. A stall that soaks whoever comes to shop will do a brisk trade exactly once.
choice What happens to the run-off? -> stripe_run
choice Good luck with the canvas. -> hub
node stripe_run
say Down a cord at the back into a bucket. I mean to find another use for the very thing that tries to drown me.
choice Good luck with the canvas. -> hub
